  "reviewNotes": [
    "Existing journal v1/stage/registry/Anchor parsers do not accept the proposed v2 formats.",
    "The present source profile lacks the SGA gate and atomic maintenance reservations; a detached signature alone does not make it migratable.",
    "SGA is separate from the five migrated owners; local files and the migrated Anchor are insufficient for independent selection.",
    "No runtime code changed. CG01-CG48 are requirements, not passing tests.",
    "Current 2-read and real-time continuous-read limitations remain; no performance improvement claimed.",
    "GenerationId is fixed before construction; built vector and SGA receipts are separate and cannot enter base/genesis/template/import-core bytes.",
    "GC requires fresh five-target verification at start and resume, continuous custody and exact batch execution binding; old Ready alone grants no deletion.",
    "Second review: source GC runs after completed; the earlier rule that the target stays read-only until GC completes is withdrawn.",
    "Current read budget has no fitted time plan; CGP must show one and readsPerGeneration before CG3."
  ],
